{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"state","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Expanding state is stored on the table using the following shape:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export type ExpandedState = true | Record<string, boolean>\n\nexport type ExpandedTableState = {\n  expanded: ExpandedState\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"row-api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Row API"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"toggleexpanded","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toggleExpanded"}]},{"type":"code","value":"toggleExpanded: (expanded?: boolean) => void","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Toggles the expanded state (or sets it if "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"expanded"},{"type":"text","value":" is provided) for the row."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getisexpanded","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getIsExpanded"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getIsExpanded: () => boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns whether the row is expanded."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getisallparentsexpanded","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getIsAllParentsExpanded"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getIsAllParentsExpanded: () => boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns whether all parent rows of the row are expanded."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getcanexpand","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getCanExpand"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getCanExpand: () => boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns whether the row can be expanded."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"gettoggleexpandedhandler","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getToggleExpandedHandler"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getToggleExpandedHandler: () => () => void","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns a function that can be used to toggle the expanded state of the row. This function can be used to bind to an event handler to a button."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"table-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Table Options"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"manualexpanding","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"manualExpanding"}]},{"type":"code","value":"manualExpanding?: boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enables manual row expansion. If this is set to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getExpandedRowModel"},{"type":"text","value":" will not be used to expand rows and you would be expected to perform the expansion in your own data model. This is useful if you are doing server-side expansion."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"onexpandedchange","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onExpandedChange"}]},{"type":"code","value":"onExpandedChange?: OnChangeFn<ExpandedState>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function is called when the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"expanded"},{"type":"text","value":" table state changes. If a function is provided, you will be responsible for managing this state on your own. To pass the managed state back to the table, use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tableOptions.state.expanded"},{"type":"text","value":" option."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"autoresetexpanded","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"autoResetExpanded"}]},{"type":"code","value":"autoResetExpanded?: boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enable this setting to automatically reset the expanded state of the table when expanding state changes."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"enableexpanding","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enableExpanding"}]},{"type":"code","value":"enableExpanding?: boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enable/disable expanding for all rows."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getexpandedrowmodel","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getExpandedRowModel"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getExpandedRowModel?: (table: Table<TData>) => () => RowModel<TData>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function is responsible for returning the expanded row model. If this function is not provided, the table will not expand rows. You can use the default exported "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getExpandedRowModel"},{"type":"text","value":" function to get the expanded row model or implement your own."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getisrowexpanded","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getIsRowExpanded"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getIsRowExpanded?: (row: Row<TData>) => boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If provided, allows you to override the default behavior of determining whether a row is currently expanded."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getrowcanexpand","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getRowCanExpand"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getRowCanExpand?: (row: Row<TData>) => boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If provided, allows you to override the default behavior of determining whether a row can be expanded."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"paginateexpandedrows","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"paginateExpandedRows"}]},{"type":"code","value":"paginateExpandedRows?: boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" expanded rows will be paginated along with the rest of the table (which means expanded rows may span multiple pages)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" expanded rows will not be considered for pagination (which means expanded rows will always render on their parents page. This also means more rows will be rendered than the set page size)"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"table-api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Table API"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"setexpanded","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setExpanded"}]},{"type":"code","value":"setExpanded: (updater: Updater<ExpandedState>) => void","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Updates the expanded state of the table via an update function or value"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"toggleallrowsexpanded","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toggleAllRowsExpanded"}]},{"type":"code","value":"toggleAllRowsExpanded: (expanded?: boolean) => void","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Toggles the expanded state for all rows. Optionally, provide a value to set the expanded state to."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"resetexpanded","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resetExpanded"}]},{"type":"code","value":"resetExpanded: (defaultState?: boolean) => void","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reset the expanded state of the table to the initial state. If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultState"},{"type":"text","value":" is provided, the expanded state will be reset to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{}"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getcansomerowsexpand","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getCanSomeRowsExpand"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getCanSomeRowsExpand: () => boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns whether there are any rows that can be expanded."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"gettoggleallrowsexpandedhandler","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getToggleAllRowsExpandedHandler"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getToggleAllRowsExpandedHandler: () => (event: unknown) => void","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns a handler that can be used to toggle the expanded state of all rows. This handler is meant to be used with an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input[type=checkbox]"},{"type":"text","value":" element."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getissomerowsexpanded","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getIsSomeRowsExpanded"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getIsSomeRowsExpanded: () => boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns whether there are any rows that are currently expanded."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getisallrowsexpanded","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getIsAllRowsExpanded"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getIsAllRowsExpanded: () => boolean","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns whether all rows are currently expanded."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getexpandeddepth","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getExpandedDepth"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getExpandedDepth: () => number","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the maximum depth of the expanded rows."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getexpandedrowmodel-2","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getExpandedRowModel"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getExpandedRowModel: () => RowModel<TData>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the row model after expansion has been applied."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getpreexpandedrowmodel","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getPreExpandedRowModel"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getPreExpandedRowModel: () => RowModel<TData>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the row model before expansion has been applied."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"state","text":"State","level":2},{"id":"row-api","text":"Row API","level":2},{"id":"toggleexpanded","text":"toggleExpanded","level":3},{"id":"getisexpanded","text":"getIsExpanded","level":3},{"id":"getisallparentsexpanded","text":"getIsAllParentsExpanded","level":3},{"id":"getcanexpand","text":"getCanExpand","level":3},{"id":"gettoggleexpandedhandler","text":"getToggleExpandedHandler","level":3},{"id":"table-options","text":"Table Options","level":2},{"id":"manualexpanding","text":"manualExpanding","level":3},{"id":"onexpandedchange","text":"onExpandedChange","level":3},{"id":"autoresetexpanded","text":"autoResetExpanded","level":3},{"id":"enableexpanding","text":"enableExpanding","level":3},{"id":"getexpandedrowmodel","text":"getExpandedRowModel","level":3},{"id":"getisrowexpanded","text":"getIsRowExpanded","level":3},{"id":"getrowcanexpand","text":"getRowCanExpand","level":3},{"id":"paginateexpandedrows","text":"paginateExpandedRows","level":3},{"id":"table-api","text":"Table API","level":2},{"id":"setexpanded","text":"setExpanded","level":3},{"id":"toggleallrowsexpanded","text":"toggleAllRowsExpanded","level":3},{"id":"resetexpanded","text":"resetExpanded","level":3},{"id":"getcansomerowsexpand","text":"getCanSomeRowsExpand","level":3},{"id":"gettoggleallrowsexpandedhandler","text":"getToggleAllRowsExpandedHandler","level":3},{"id":"getissomerowsexpanded","text":"getIsSomeRowsExpanded","level":3},{"id":"getisallrowsexpanded","text":"getIsAllRowsExpanded","level":3},{"id":"getexpandeddepth","text":"getExpandedDepth","level":3},{"id":"getexpandedrowmodel-2","text":"getExpandedRowModel","level":3},{"id":"getpreexpandedrowmodel","text":"getPreExpandedRowModel","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n## State\n\nExpanding state is stored on the table using the following shape:\n\n```tsx\nexport type ExpandedState = true | Record<string, boolean>\n\nexport type ExpandedTableState = {\n  expanded: ExpandedState\n}\n```\n\n## Row API\n\n### `toggleExpanded`\n\n```tsx\ntoggleExpanded: (expanded?: boolean) => void\n```\n\nToggles the expanded state (or sets it if `expanded` is provided) for the row.\n\n### `getIsExpanded`\n\n```tsx\ngetIsExpanded: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether the row is expanded.\n\n### `getIsAllParentsExpanded`\n\n```tsx\ngetIsAllParentsExpanded: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether all parent rows of the row are expanded.\n\n### `getCanExpand`\n\n```tsx\ngetCanExpand: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether the row can be expanded.\n\n### `getToggleExpandedHandler`\n\n```tsx\ngetToggleExpandedHandler: () => () => void\n```\n\nReturns a function that can be used to toggle the expanded state of the row. This function can be used to bind to an event handler to a button.\n\n## Table Options\n\n### `manualExpanding`\n\n```tsx\nmanualExpanding?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables manual row expansion. If this is set to `true`, `getExpandedRowModel` will not be used to expand rows and you would be expected to perform the expansion in your own data model. This is useful if you are doing server-side expansion.\n\n### `onExpandedChange`\n\n```tsx\nonExpandedChange?: OnChangeFn<ExpandedState>\n```\n\nThis function is called when the `expanded` table state changes. If a function is provided, you will be responsible for managing this state on your own. To pass the managed state back to the table, use the `tableOptions.state.expanded` option.\n\n### `autoResetExpanded`\n\n```tsx\nautoResetExpanded?: boolean\n```\n\nEnable this setting to automatically reset the expanded state of the table when expanding state changes.\n\n### `enableExpanding`\n\n```tsx\nenableExpanding?: boolean\n```\n\nEnable/disable expanding for all rows.\n\n### `getExpandedRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ngetExpandedRowModel?: (table: Table<TData>) => () => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\nThis function is responsible for returning the expanded row model. If this function is not provided, the table will not expand rows. You can use the default exported `getExpandedRowModel` function to get the expanded row model or implement your own.\n\n### `getIsRowExpanded`\n\n```tsx\ngetIsRowExpanded?: (row: Row<TData>) => boolean\n```\n\nIf provided, allows you to override the default behavior of determining whether a row is currently expanded.\n\n### `getRowCanExpand`\n\n```tsx\ngetRowCanExpand?: (row: Row<TData>) => boolean\n```\n\nIf provided, allows you to override the default behavior of determining whether a row can be expanded.\n\n### `paginateExpandedRows`\n\n```tsx\npaginateExpandedRows?: boolean\n```\n\nIf `true` expanded rows will be paginated along with the rest of the table (which means expanded rows may span multiple pages).\n\nIf `false` expanded rows will not be considered for pagination (which means expanded rows will always render on their parents page. This also means more rows will be rendered than the set page size)\n\n## Table API\n\n### `setExpanded`\n\n```tsx\nsetExpanded: (updater: Updater<ExpandedState>) => void\n```\n\nUpdates the expanded state of the table via an update function or value\n\n### `toggleAllRowsExpanded`\n\n```tsx\ntoggleAllRowsExpanded: (expanded?: boolean) => void\n```\n\nToggles the expanded state for all rows. Optionally, provide a value to set the expanded state to.\n\n### `resetExpanded`\n\n```tsx\nresetExpanded: (defaultState?: boolean) => void\n```\n\nReset the expanded state of the table to the initial state. If `defaultState` is provided, the expanded state will be reset to `{}`\n\n### `getCanSomeRowsExpand`\n\n```tsx\ngetCanSomeRowsExpand: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether there are any rows that can be expanded.\n\n### `getToggleAllRowsExpandedHandler`\n\n```tsx\ngetToggleAllRowsExpandedHandler: () => (event: unknown) => void\n```\n\nReturns a handler that can be used to toggle the expanded state of all rows. This handler is meant to be used with an `input[type=checkbox]` element.\n\n### `getIsSomeRowsExpanded`\n\n```tsx\ngetIsSomeRowsExpanded: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether there are any rows that are currently expanded.\n\n### `getIsAllRowsExpanded`\n\n```tsx\ngetIsAllRowsExpanded: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether all rows are currently expanded.\n\n### `getExpandedDepth`\n\n```tsx\ngetExpandedDepth: () => number\n```\n\nReturns the maximum depth of the expanded rows.\n\n### `getExpandedRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ngetExpandedRowModel: () => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\nReturns the row model after expansion has been applied.\n\n### `getPreExpandedRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ngetPreExpandedRowModel: () => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\nReturns the row model before expansion has been applied.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Expanding APIs\nid: expanding\n---\n\n## State\n\nExpanding state is stored on the table using the following shape:\n\n```tsx\nexport type ExpandedState = true | Record<string, boolean>\n\nexport type ExpandedTableState = {\n  expanded: ExpandedState\n}\n```\n\n## Row API\n\n### `toggleExpanded`\n\n```tsx\ntoggleExpanded: (expanded?: boolean) => void\n```\n\nToggles the expanded state (or sets it if `expanded` is provided) for the row.\n\n### `getIsExpanded`\n\n```tsx\ngetIsExpanded: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether the row is expanded.\n\n### `getIsAllParentsExpanded`\n\n```tsx\ngetIsAllParentsExpanded: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether all parent rows of the row are expanded.\n\n### `getCanExpand`\n\n```tsx\ngetCanExpand: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether the row can be expanded.\n\n### `getToggleExpandedHandler`\n\n```tsx\ngetToggleExpandedHandler: () => () => void\n```\n\nReturns a function that can be used to toggle the expanded state of the row. This function can be used to bind to an event handler to a button.\n\n## Table Options\n\n### `manualExpanding`\n\n```tsx\nmanualExpanding?: boolean\n```\n\nEnables manual row expansion. If this is set to `true`, `getExpandedRowModel` will not be used to expand rows and you would be expected to perform the expansion in your own data model. This is useful if you are doing server-side expansion.\n\n### `onExpandedChange`\n\n```tsx\nonExpandedChange?: OnChangeFn<ExpandedState>\n```\n\nThis function is called when the `expanded` table state changes. If a function is provided, you will be responsible for managing this state on your own. To pass the managed state back to the table, use the `tableOptions.state.expanded` option.\n\n### `autoResetExpanded`\n\n```tsx\nautoResetExpanded?: boolean\n```\n\nEnable this setting to automatically reset the expanded state of the table when expanding state changes.\n\n### `enableExpanding`\n\n```tsx\nenableExpanding?: boolean\n```\n\nEnable/disable expanding for all rows.\n\n### `getExpandedRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ngetExpandedRowModel?: (table: Table<TData>) => () => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\nThis function is responsible for returning the expanded row model. If this function is not provided, the table will not expand rows. You can use the default exported `getExpandedRowModel` function to get the expanded row model or implement your own.\n\n### `getIsRowExpanded`\n\n```tsx\ngetIsRowExpanded?: (row: Row<TData>) => boolean\n```\n\nIf provided, allows you to override the default behavior of determining whether a row is currently expanded.\n\n### `getRowCanExpand`\n\n```tsx\ngetRowCanExpand?: (row: Row<TData>) => boolean\n```\n\nIf provided, allows you to override the default behavior of determining whether a row can be expanded.\n\n### `paginateExpandedRows`\n\n```tsx\npaginateExpandedRows?: boolean\n```\n\nIf `true` expanded rows will be paginated along with the rest of the table (which means expanded rows may span multiple pages).\n\nIf `false` expanded rows will not be considered for pagination (which means expanded rows will always render on their parents page. This also means more rows will be rendered than the set page size)\n\n## Table API\n\n### `setExpanded`\n\n```tsx\nsetExpanded: (updater: Updater<ExpandedState>) => void\n```\n\nUpdates the expanded state of the table via an update function or value\n\n### `toggleAllRowsExpanded`\n\n```tsx\ntoggleAllRowsExpanded: (expanded?: boolean) => void\n```\n\nToggles the expanded state for all rows. Optionally, provide a value to set the expanded state to.\n\n### `resetExpanded`\n\n```tsx\nresetExpanded: (defaultState?: boolean) => void\n```\n\nReset the expanded state of the table to the initial state. If `defaultState` is provided, the expanded state will be reset to `{}`\n\n### `getCanSomeRowsExpand`\n\n```tsx\ngetCanSomeRowsExpand: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether there are any rows that can be expanded.\n\n### `getToggleAllRowsExpandedHandler`\n\n```tsx\ngetToggleAllRowsExpandedHandler: () => (event: unknown) => void\n```\n\nReturns a handler that can be used to toggle the expanded state of all rows. This handler is meant to be used with an `input[type=checkbox]` element.\n\n### `getIsSomeRowsExpanded`\n\n```tsx\ngetIsSomeRowsExpanded: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether there are any rows that are currently expanded.\n\n### `getIsAllRowsExpanded`\n\n```tsx\ngetIsAllRowsExpanded: () => boolean\n```\n\nReturns whether all rows are currently expanded.\n\n### `getExpandedDepth`\n\n```tsx\ngetExpandedDepth: () => number\n```\n\nReturns the maximum depth of the expanded rows.\n\n### `getExpandedRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ngetExpandedRowModel: () => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\nReturns the row model after expansion has been applied.\n\n### `getPreExpandedRowModel`\n\n```tsx\ngetPreExpandedRowModel: () => RowModel<TData>\n```\n\nReturns the row model before expansion has been applied.\n"}
